"DOI":"10.1515\/zna-1972-0303","volume":"27a","author":"Moon","year":"1972","journal-title":"Z. Naturforsch."},{"key":"10.1016\/S0304-3991(85)80008-5_bib16","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"423","DOI":"10.1016\/0039-6028(81)90649-X","volume":"110","author":"Maksym","year":"1981","journal-title":"Surface Sci"}],"container-title":["Ultramicroscopy"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S0304399185800085?httpAccept=text\/xml","content-type":"text\/xml","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S0304399185800085?httpAccept=text\/plain","content-type":"text\/plain","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2021,7,13]],"date-time":"2021-07-13T15:59:02Z","timestamp":1626191942000},"score":57.932507,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/linkinghub.elsevier.com\/retrieve\/pii\/S0304399185800085"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[1985,1]]},"references-count":16,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-print":{"date-parts":[[1985,1]]}},"alternative-id":["S0304399185800085"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/s0304-3991(85)80008-5","ISSN":["0304-3991"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0304-3991","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[1985,1]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,4,1]],"date-time":"2022-04-01T11:20:40Z","timestamp":1648812040832},"reference-count":7,"publisher":"Cambridge University Press (CUP)","issue":"1","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]],"date-time":"2020-06-18T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1592438400000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":10903,"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/terms"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Proc. annu. meet. Electron Microsc. Soc. Am."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1990,8,12]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>In order to increase intensity and contrast in the image of a surface, the surface resonance conditions have been widely used to enhance the Bragg reflection for image formation in REM (Reflection Electron Microscopy). However, detailed studies of how the resonance conditions relate to the imaging contrast have not been reported. This paper will concentrate on the general properties of the different resonance conditions, as well as the resulting image contrast.<\/jats:p><jats:p>Figure 1 shows a series of RHEED (Reflection High Energy Electron Diffraction) patterns and REM images from the same region of a Pt(l11) surface with the incident electron beam in a direction close to the [112] zone axis at 200 KeV, with a glancing incident angle of about 24 mrad which corresponds to the (555) Bragg reflection condition inside the crystal. For the purpose of convenience in discussion, the four different diffraction conditions shown in figures l(al)-(dl) have been named as D1-D4. With Dl, the specular reflected spot falls in an intersection of a parallel Kikuchi line with a parabola; with D2, the specular reflected spot coincides with an intersection of the Kikuchi lines running parallel to and inclined to the crystal surface; with D3, the specular reflected spot crosses only the parallel Kikuchi line; and with D4, the specular reflected spot intersects only with a parabola. It was found that the diffraction conditions Dl and D2 can not be considered as identical, although the specular reflected spots for both cases are commonly regarded as (555) Bragg reflection in the RHEED pattern. Detailed inspection indicates that for Dl, both the Bragg reflection and the electron surface channelling wave are excited, and for D2, the excitement of simultaneous Bragg reflection occurs closely associated with the properties of three-dimensional dynamical diffraction for a bulk crystal.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1017\/s0424820100180410","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]],"date-time":"2020-06-18T11:08:49Z","timestamp":1592478529000},"page":"332-333","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Characterization of Surface Resonance Conditions for Surface Imaging"],"prefix":"10.1017","volume":"48","author":[{"given":"Nan","family":"Yao","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"John M.","family":"Cowley","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"56","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]]},"reference":[{"key":"S0424820100180410_ref07","unstructured":"7 This work was supported by NSF grant DMR88-10238 and made use of the resources of the ASU"},{"key":"S0424820100180410_ref05","unstructured":"5 Yao, N. and Cowley, J. M. , in this proceeding."},{"key":"S0424820100180410_ref01","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"424","DOI":"10.1016\/0039-6028(81)90038-8","volume":"102","author":"Osakabe","year":"1981","journal-title":"Surface Science"},{"key":"S0424820100180410_ref04","author":"Yao","year":"1990","journal-title":"Surface Science"},{"key":"S0424820100180410_ref03","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0304-3991(89)90244-1"},{"key":"S0424820100180410_ref02","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/0304-3991(83)90004-9"},{"key":"S0424820100180410_ref06","author":"Yao","year":"1990","journal-title":"J. Electron Micro. Tech."}],"container-title":["Proceedings, annual meeting, Electron Microscopy Society of America"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/services\/aop-cambridge-core\/content\/view\/S0424820100180410","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2020,6,18]],"date-time":"2020-06-18T11:27:01Z","timestamp":1592479621000},"score":57.30503,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.cambridge.org\/core\/product\/identifier\/S0424820100180410\/type\/journal_article"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[1990,8,12]]},"references-count":7,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-print":{"date-parts":[[1990,8,12]]}},"alternative-id":["S0424820100180410"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/s0424820100180410","ISSN":["0424-8201","2690-1315"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0424-8201","type":"print"},{"value":"2690-1315","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[1990,8,12]]}}],"items-per-page":5,"query":{"start-index":0,"search-terms":null}}}